-- =========================================================================
-- Ecom capabilities — `Messaging` + `Payment`, authored as Fenel
-- record-of-methods types (signature-substrate Phase 4-prep, D0b: the ecom
-- TS `Interface` literals consolidate onto this module-local source — the
-- ai/email `capability.fenel` playbook; `design/unified-dispatch.md`
-- "typeclasses ARE types").
--
-- A capability is a record whose fields are its methods (each an arrow
-- type). The ecom seam reads these types and `seedFromType`s them into the
-- dispatch seeds (replacing the retired hand-written consts). Both are
-- NOMINAL — dispatched by PROVIDER NAME via `resolveCapabilityMethod`
-- (which splits a qualified `Messaging.<method>` / `Payment.<method>`
-- action and picks the highest-priority provider instance); no method
-- carries the class type-param in argument position, so the derived seed
-- needs only the right method NAMEs + signatures.
--
-- The arrows mirror the retired TS literals (the LIVE contracts):
--   Messaging.send            to String -> body String -> subject String
--                             -> template String -> {}
--   Payment.create_checkout   amount Number -> currency String -> plan
--                             String -> metadata {} -> {}
--   Payment.verify            payment_id String -> {}
--   Payment.refund            payment_id String -> amount Number -> {}
-- The `{}` returns/params ride along verbatim (parity; the documented
-- anti-pattern, not "fixed" here). Param NAMES + per-method labels and the
-- capability descriptions are display metadata the curried spelling drops —
-- the SAME authorized delta the AI capability port already established
-- (`fenel/modules/ai/capability.fenel` header); the retired spellings are
-- recorded above for the record.
--
-- This file is loaded SEPARATELY from `types.fenel` (NOT merged) so the
-- capability types do NOT enter `ecomModule.entities`; the seam reads only
-- their types to derive the seeds. Names kept byte-identical.
-- =========================================================================

Messaging = Messaging send: (String -> String -> String -> String -> {})

Payment = Payment create_checkout: (Number -> String -> String -> {} -> {}) verify: (String -> {}) refund: (String -> Number -> {})
